---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';

const page = {
    "title": "Hi-Fi Spacesuit | xdd44's Collections",
    "description": "Hi-Fi spacesuit, designed to deliver vibration therapy to key muscle groups and bones, developed in MIT's Space Architecture course.",
    "image": "https://xdd44.xyz/image/Architecture/Hi-Fi/Cover.jpg",
    "heading": "Hi-Fi Spacesuit",
    "cover": "image/Architecture/Hi-Fi/Cover2.jpg",
    "category": "Architecture",
    "year": "2025",
    "tags": [
        "MIT Space Architecture",
        "Spacesuit",
        "Group Project"
    ]
};
---

<ProjectLayout {...page}>
    <p>Group project, MAS.S66/4.154/16.89 Space Architecture, MIT Master of Architecture</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.media.mit.edu/courses/mas-s66/"><strong>Course overview and instructors</strong></a></p>
    <p><strong>Team members:</strong> Mateo, <strong>xdd</strong>, Farida, Nara</p>
    <p>Exhibited in summer 2026 at <a href="https://www.exploratorium.edu/visit/calendar/space" target="_blank">Life in Space, Exploratorium</a>, San Francisco</p>

    <figure class="project-figure wide"><img src="image/Architecture/Hi-Fi/Cover.jpg" alt="Final Model"><figcaption>Photo of the suit at the exhibition</figcaption></figure>

    <p>Bones and muscles grow weak in the weightlessness of space. One way to counteract this is vibration therapy-stimulating bone and muscle cells by shaking them. This suit, designed to be worn inside a space station or habitat, features strategically placed vibrating pads that deliver vibration therapy to key muscle groups and bones.</p>

    <figure class="project-figure wide"><img src="image/Architecture/Hi-Fi/Detail.jpg" alt="Final Model"><figcaption>Detail</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="project-figure wide"><img src="image/Architecture/Hi-Fi/Liquid.jpg" alt="Final Model"><figcaption>Early Prototype sponsored by <a href="https://www.rapidliquidprint.com/" target="_blank">Rapid Liquid Print</a></figcaption></figure>
</ProjectLayout>
